ng:Christian_Slater_award_received_Golden_Globe_Award a sem:Event ;
    ng:object "Golden Globe Award" ;
    ng:property "award received" ;
    ng:subject "Christian Slater" ;
    sem:hasTimeStamp "2016-01-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:comment "Christian Michael Leonard Slater (born August 18, 1969) is an American actor. He made his film debut with a leading role in The Legend of Billie Jean (1985) and gained wider recognition for his breakout role as Jason \"J.D.\" Dean, a sociopathic high school student, in the satire Heathers (1989). In the 1990s, Slater starred in a number of big-budget films, including Young Guns II (1990), Robin Hood: Prince of Thieves (1991), Interview with the Vampire (1994), Broken Arrow (1996), and Hard Rain (1998) as well as cult films like Gleaming the Cube (1989), Pump Up the Volume (1990) and" .

ng:Chuck_Abbott_award_received_Disney_Legends a sem:Event ;
    ng:object "Disney Legends" ;
    ng:property "award received" ;
    ng:subject "Chuck Abbott" ;
    sem:hasTimeStamp "2005-01-01"^^xsd:date .

ng:Claire_Danes_award_received_Golden_Globe_Award a sem:Event ;
    ng:object "Golden Globe Award" ;
    ng:property "award received" ;
    ng:subject "Claire Danes" ;
    sem:hasTimeStamp "1979-04-12"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:comment "Claire Catherine Danes (born April 12, 1979) is an American actor. Prolific in film and television since her teens, she is the recipient of three Primetime Emmy Awards and four Golden Globe Awards. In 2012 and 2026, Time named her one of the 100 most influential people in the world." .

ng:Claire_Foy_award_received_Golden_Globe_Award a sem:Event ;
    ng:object "Golden Globe Award" ;
    ng:property "award received" ;
    ng:subject "Claire Foy" ;
    sem:hasTimeStamp "2017-01-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:comment "Claire Elizabeth Foy (born 16 April 1984) is a British actress. She is best known for her portrayal of Queen Elizabeth II in the Netflix series The Crown (2016–2017, 2020, 2022–2023), for which she received various accolades such as a Golden Globe and two Primetime Emmy Awards. Foy made her screen debut in the pilot episode of the supernatural comedy series Being Human (2008)." .

ng:Clarence_Nash_award_received_Disney_Legends a sem:Event ;
    ng:object "Disney Legends" ;
    ng:property "award received" ;
    ng:subject "Clarence Nash" ;
    sem:hasTimeStamp "1993-01-01"^^xsd:date .

ng:Claude_Coats_award_received_Disney_Legends a sem:Event ;
    ng:object "Disney Legends" ;
    ng:property "award received" ;
    ng:subject "Claude Coats" ;
    sem:hasTimeStamp "1991-01-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:comment "Claude Coats (January 17, 1913 – January 9, 1992) was an American artist, background artist, animator and set designer, known for his work with the Walt Disney Animation Studios and Walt Disney Imagineering. His pioneering work with the company helped define the character of animated films, and later, immersive installations with his designs for Disneyland. Coats, known as \"The Gentle Giant\" was inducted a Disney Legend in 1991." .

ng:Cliff_Edwards_award_received_Disney_Legends a sem:Event ;
    ng:object "Disney Legends" ;
    ng:property "award received" ;
    ng:subject "Cliff Edwards" ;
    sem:hasTimeStamp "2000-01-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:comment "Cliff Edwards (June 14, 1895 – July 17, 1971), nicknamed \"Ukulele Ike\", was an American pop singer, musician and actor. He enjoyed considerable popularity in the 1920s and early 1930s, specializing in jazzy renditions of pop standards and novelty tunes, including \"Singin' in the Rain\" in 1929. Later in his career, he appeared in films and did voices for animated cartoons, and is well-remembered as the voice of Jiminy Cricket in Walt Disney's Pinocchio (1940) (introducing the standard \"When You Wish Upon a Star\") and Fun and Fancy Free (1947), and Dandy Crow in Walt Disney's Dumbo (1941)." .

ng:Clint_Eastwood_award_received_Golden_Globe_Award a sem:Event ;
    ng:object "Golden Globe Award" ;
    ng:property "award received" ;
    ng:subject "Clint Eastwood" ;
    sem:hasTimeStamp "1989-01-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:comment "Clinton Eastwood Jr. (born May 31, 1930) is a retired American actor, filmmaker, and musician. After achieving success in the Western TV series Rawhide, Eastwood rose to international fame with his role as the \"Man with No Name\" in Sergio Leone's Dollars Trilogy of spaghetti Westerns during the mid-1960s and as antihero cop Harry Callahan in the five Dirty Harry films throughout the 1970s and 1980s. These roles, among others, have made Eastwood an enduring cultural icon of masculinity." .

ng:Clyde_Geronimi_award_received_Disney_Legends a sem:Event ;
    ng:object "Disney Legends" ;
    ng:property "award received" ;
    ng:subject "Clyde Geronimi" ;
