    ng:property "award received" ;
    ng:subject "James Gandolfini" ;
    sem:hasTimeStamp "2000-01-01"^^xsd:date ;
    rdfs:comment "James John Gandolfini (Italian: [ɡandolˈfiːni]; September 18, 1961&#160;– June 19, 2013) was an American actor. He was best known for his portrayal of Tony Soprano, the Italian-American mafia crime boss in HBO's television series The Sopranos (1999–2007). For this role, he won three Primetime Emmy Awards, five Actor Awards, and one Golden Globe Award." .

